* Symptoms include low back pain aggravated by cold, difficulty turning, dark tongue with white greasy coating (cold-dampness and blood stasis pattern); stabbing pain with fixed location, tenderness on pressure, worse at night and milder in the daytime (blood stasis low back pain); dull lingering low back pain with soreness and weakness, persistent symptoms, local cold sensation, preference for warmth and pressure, worsening upon cold exposure, cold limbs (kidney-yang deficiency low back pain);
